    {
      "id": "c15044398d2055ec5d027d0d25c62218ffa91484",
      "individual_note": false,
      "resolvable": true,
      "resolved": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 676252461,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "For packet details we have selection and hover as separate and simultaneous actions (dark blue and light blue), I think it that should be reflected in the bytes view.\n\n@rknall If I understand correctly Ctrl+click now locks the byte selection (that's nice), but then you should remove the previous behaviour of locking without the Ctrl modifier.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jvalverde"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-09-13T16:32:04.405Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-09-13T19:44:57.434Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 116598319,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 4178,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 676394427,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Historically both views where separate in handling and moving them to the same behavior would change quite a bit. Ctrl+\"Mouse Move\" will prevent the hover mechanism, not locking in the selection mechanism. That will be done via the context menu option",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9e1d973c5007651b2ca47071f80324c2de5349d873e365cf0761df5542dfe382?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rknall"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-09-13T19:44:57.379Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-09-13T19:44:57.379Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 116598319,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": false,
          "resolved_by": null,
          "resolved_at": null,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 4178,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 676566867,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I had misunderstood your change, I thought the behavior of Ctrl+click was modified, but it's not. Only the hover is modified by Ctrl.\n\nA single click on the bytes pane does the same thing (hover prevention, it's a toggle). This was introduced for \"keeping the bearings\". If I had known how to use modifier keys at the time I'd probably have used Ctrl+click instead.\n\nI believe it used to have hover also in addition to the selection, but I think that was removed by @geraldcombs at some point, because yellow offered a terrible contrast. I hope I'm not misremembering that.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jvalverde"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-09-14T03:41:38.244Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-09-14T03:41:38.244Z",
          "system": false,
